   "doc": "Diagnostics, log only: the decode ring's peers kernel records, for each exchange and peer, the sequence and, on the GPU's own clock, when the kernel started, when that peer's words were all in and when the copy-out ended (a ring of 8,192 records in device memory, 256 KiB); each rank writes roci-xlog-rank<R>.txt when its ring closes. Per rank, wait and copy-out are then exact (one clock), and captures from the four ranks pair on the sequence instead of by time. Costs a few stores, two clock reads and one block barrier on each exchange's copy-out when on, nothing when off. Replies unchanged.",
